│ patch_type               │ fix                                                                                       │
│ patch_name               │ collapse_fix_loosened_regularization                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ The validation failure shows a critical issue: **pred_std_ratio=0.0091**, which is far    │
│                          │ below the MIN_PRED_STD_RATIO threshold of 0.15. This indicates severe **prediction        │
│                          │ collapse** — the model is predicting values very close to the mean instead of capturing   │
│                          │ signal variance.                                                                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Root cause analysis:                                                                      │
│                          │ - The collapse penalty of 0.705 is the dominant penalty, indicating the model's output    │
│                          │ variance is only ~0.91% of the actual variance                                            │
│                          │ - The model is over-regularized: high min_child_weight (10), high reg_alpha (0.1), high   │
│                          │ reg_lambda (1.0), and low learning_rate (0.01) with only 300 estimators                   │
│                          │ - These hyperparameters are too restrictive for a forecasting task that needs to capture  │
│                          │ real directional signal                                                                   │
│                          │ - Features are being built but the model cannot express them due to excessive             │
│                          │ regularization                                                                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The fix:                                                                                  │
│                          │ 1. **Dramatically reduce regularization**: Lower reg_alpha and reg_lambda to allow the    │
│                          │ model to learn feature signals                                                            │
│                          │ 2. **Increase model capacity**: Raise n_estimators to 500 and increase max_depth to 5-6   │
│                          │ to capture non-linear patterns                                                            │
│                          │ 3. **Reduce min_child_weight**: Lower from 10 to 3 to allow splits on smaller samples     │
│                          │ 4. **Increase learning_rate**: Raise from 0.01 to 0.05 so the model can adjust more       │
│                          │ aggressively                                                                              │
│                          │ 5. **Increase subsample and colsample**: Both were conservative; raise to improve         │
│                          │ exploration                                                                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ These changes will allow the model to express the feature signals without overfitting     │
│                          │ (the overfit_gap is only 0.013, indicating no overfitting issue currently).               │
