│ patch_description        │ The program suffered from prediction collapse (pred_std_ratio=0.0091 vs target 0.15+) due │
│                          │ to:                                                                                       │
│                          │ 1. Over-regularization (reg_lambda=1.0, reg_alpha=0.1, min_child_weight=10 were too       │
│                          │ strict)                                                                                   │
│                          │ 2. Insufficient model capacity (n_estimators=300, learning_rate=0.01 too conservative)    │
│                          │ 3. Feature alignment bug: build_features() called dropna() which removed rows, breaking   │
│                          │ alignment between X and y                                                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The fix:                                                                                  │
│                          │ - Remove dropna() from build_features(), instead forward-fill NaN values to preserve      │
│                          │ alignment                                                                                 │
│                          │ - Drastically reduce regularization (reg_alpha=0, reg_lambda=0.1)                         │
│                          │ - Reduce min_child_weight from 10 to 1                                                    │
│                          │ - Increase learning_rate from 0.01 to 0.05                                                │
│                          │ - Increase n_estimators from 300 to 500                                                   │
│                          │ - Fill remaining NaN with 0 instead of dropping rows                                      │
