│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ fix                                                                                       │
│ patch_name               │ less_regularization_shifted_features                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ The validation output shows a classic prediction-collapse issue: `pred_std_ratio=0.0091`  │
│                          │ is far too low, meaning the model is predicting near the mean almost all the time. The    │
│                          │ current XGBoost setup is over-regularized for this task (`min_child_weight=10`,           │
│                          │ `reg_alpha=0.1`, `reg_lambda=1.0`, `learning_rate=0.01` with only 300 trees), so the      │
│                          │ model lacks expressivity and underfits.                                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ I fixed this by:                                                                          │
│                          │ 1. Making all engineered features explicitly past-only using a 1-bar shift before any     │
│                          │ rolling/technical calculations, which also aligns with the stated no-lookahead            │
│                          │ constraint.                                                                               │
│                          │ 2. Expanding the feature set modestly with a few useful regime and interaction features   │
│                          │ while keeping total feature count under 80.                                               │
│                          │ 3. Reducing regularization and increasing model capacity so predictions are less          │
│                          │ collapsed:                                                                                │
│                          │    - lower `min_child_weight`                                                             │
│                          │    - lower `reg_alpha` / `reg_lambda`                                                     │
│                          │    - deeper trees                                                                         │
│                          │    - more estimators                                                                      │
│                          │    - slightly higher learning rate                                                        │
│                          │ 4. Keeping the interface and return format unchanged.                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This should increase prediction variance and improve directional accuracy without peeking │
│                          │ at future data.                                                                           │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
