│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ fix                                                                                       │
│ patch_name               │ increase_expressivity_and_technical_features                                              │
│ patch_description        │ The model failed because its predictions "collapsed towards the mean"                     │
│                          │ (pred_std_ratio=0.0091), which is far below the required 0.15 threshold. This typically   │
│                          │ occurs when a model is either too under-expressive or too heavily regularized given the   │
│                          │ signal-to-noise ratio of the data.                                                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ To fix this, I made the following adjustments:                                            │
│                          │ 1.  **Increased XGBoost Expressivity:** I raised the `learning_rate` from 0.01 to 0.05    │
│                          │ and increased `max_depth` from 4 to 6. I significantly lowered `min_child_weight` from 10 │
│                          │ to 1, which allows the model to create more granular splits and capture more variance in  │
│                          │ the target. I also increased `n_estimators` with a longer `early_stopping_rounds` to      │
│                          │ ensure the model converges on more complex patterns.                                      │
│                          │ 2.  **Enhanced Feature Engineering:** I expanded the feature set to better capture        │
│                          │ momentum and mean-reversion. I added distance-from-moving-average features (MA Dist),     │
│                          │ more granular return lags (log-returns), MACD histogram, and normalized volume z-scores.  │
│                          │ 3.  **Removed Potential Bottlenecks:** I removed the slow `df.apply` OBI logic to ensure  │
│                          │ execution stays well within the 3-minute constraint, focusing on high-quality vectorized  │
│                          │ OHLCV and funding features instead.                                                       │
│                          │ 4.  **Improved Robustness:** Added ffill() and better cleaning to handle NaNs             │
│                          │ consistently.                                                                             │
