│ patch_type               │ fix                                                                                       │
│ patch_name               │ fix_prediction_collapse_and_alignment                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ The model was collapsing predictions toward the mean (pred_std_ratio=0.0091) due to two   │
│                          │ critical issues:                                                                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **Data alignment bug**: `feat.dropna()` was dropping all rows containing any NaN       │
│                          │ values. Since rolling window features require warmup periods (e.g., RSI-14 needs 14 bars, │
│                          │ volatility-60 needs 60 bars), and orderbook/funding data may have sparse NaNs, this was   │
│                          │ dropping the majority of the training data and causing severe misalignment with targets.  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **Over-regularization**: The hyperparameters (reg_alpha=0.1, reg_lambda=1.0,           │
│                          │ min_child_weight=10, n_estimators=300 with learning_rate=0.01) were too conservative,     │
│                          │ suppressing model expressivity.                                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **Fix**: Replace `dropna()` with forward-fill to preserve row alignment, and              │
│                          │ significantly loosen regularization while increasing model capacity. This allows the      │
│                          │ model to learn real trading signals instead of defaulting to the mean.                    │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
