│ patch_type               │ fix                                                                                       │
│ patch_name               │ fix_fillna_type_and_expressivity                                                          │
│ patch_description        │ The bug was caused by an incompatible signature in `pd.DataFrame.fillna()`, where the     │
│                          │ `method` argument is deprecated/removed in newer versions of pandas. The fix replaces     │
│                          │ `.fillna(method='ffill')` and `.fillna(method='bfill')` with the modern `.ffill()` and    │
│                          │ `.bfill()` methods.                                                                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Additionally, to address the common failure mode of model collapse (where                 │
│                          │ `pred_std_ratio` is too low), I loosened the regularization and increased model           │
│                          │ expressivity by reducing `min_child_weight` and adjusting `reg_lambda`/`reg_alpha`. I     │
│                          │ also expanded the feature set to include EMA-distance signals and momentum oscillators    │
│                          │ (total features = 34), which should provide stronger signals to reach the 0.52            │
│                          │ Directional Accuracy (DA) target.                                                         │
